<task id="228" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Subscription + Dataverse environment become manual prerequisites: intake requires both (and containerTypeId); H1 proves the subscription is the customer's own; H5 adopts the operator's environment and never creates one; H10 runs before H6; Model 1 deploys the customer stamp</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T228 (D4, Q1, G3, G19)</phase>
    <gate>after 227g (✅)</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>L2 API intake + handlers H1/H5/H10 + DAG + ARM runner, Bicep RBAC, schema/prereqs, the operator skill, binding docs; security-relevant (subscription Owner grant, cross-customer adoption guards).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting provisioning-pipeline change with isolation guards and a DAG reorder.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits .claude/constraints and the provision-environment skill (main-session-only).</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, dataverse, bicep, model1-dedicated, tenant-isolation, testing</tags>
    <deps>227g</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the customer's Azure subscription and Dataverse environment operator-created prerequisites that L2 verifies and adopts, so Model 1 runs can be dispatched.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, ARM, Dataverse Web API, Bicep, operator skill).</role>

  <goal>
    D4/Q1 (owner): the operator creates the customer's subscription and Dataverse environment; L2 never creates either.
    Owner decision 2026-10-06: the L2 identity holds **Owner** on each customer subscription (customer.bicep writes role
    assignments; Contributor cannot). After this task a Model 1 run goes intake → H0 … H13 with no shared or default
    subscription anywhere, and a run can never act on another customer's subscription or environment.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Mapped 2026-10-06: there is NO server-side shared subscription — Model 1 without `subscriptionId` silently used the
      operator's `az account show` subscription (skill Step 4.0). H5 creates the environment through the BAP admin API
      (BapRestEnvironmentCreator) and reads `region`/`tier`, which the skill fills with an Azure region and the COST tier.
      The run DAG has H10 (makes the BFF app registration a Dataverse application user) AFTER H7, while H6 and H7 already
      sign in to Dataverse as that app registration — so H6 would be refused in any environment it did not create. H8 and
      H10 read/write the environment as the L2 Worker identity, which previously had access only as the BAP creator.
      ArmDeploymentRunner's Model 1 arm throws (T225a). controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep grants the L2 UAMI Contributor on
      the PLATFORM subscription ("fleet") — under D-12 no stamp lives there.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Api/Api/RunsEndpoints.cs (ISH-02 498-527; pairing 1130-1187); Core/Models/IntakeParameterCatalog.cs</file>
      <file>Core/Handlers/SubscriptionReadiness/{H1SubscriptionReadinessHandler,ArmSubscriptionReadinessProbe}.cs</file>
      <file>Core/Handlers/DataverseEnvCreation/** (H5, BapRestEnvironmentCreator, IDataverseEnvCreator, PacAdmin…, DataverseWebApiHealthProbe, options); Worker/Program.cs registrations; Core/Handlers/Preflight/BapRestEnvironmentRateProbe.cs</file>
      <file>Core/Reconciler/{DagAdvancer,HandlerRunInputs}.cs; Core/Handlers/BicepInfraDeploy/ArmDeploymentRunner.cs</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/{platform-controlplane.bicep,modules/controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep}</file>
      <file>scripts/provisioning-prereqs/{intake.schema.json,prereqs.yaml,context-defaults.*.json}; .claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md §2.3/§2.4/§3/§5/§7.2/§7.4; docs/architecture/SPAARKE-ENVIRONMENT-RESOURCE-INVENTORY.md; .claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-027-subscription-isolation-and-dataverse-solution-management.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">No default, shared or ambient subscription anywhere (server, schema, skill). L2 creates no subscription and no Dataverse environment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">The L2 identity's per-customer grant is Owner on that subscription, granted by the operator (repurposed controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep, deployed at the customer subscription); remove the platform-subscription grant from platform-controlplane.bicep. Never run a live role change here — the module and its runbook step only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="isolation">H1 refuses a subscription outside the run's tenant or holding another customer's `rg-spaarke-{otherId}-*` resource group; H5 refuses an environment whose host does not belong to this customer (`spaarke-{customerId}` or `spaarke-{customerId}-{environmentName}`). Refusals are Resumable and name what they found; nothing is written.</constraint>
    <constraint source="needed-or-remove">Code that only served environment creation goes (BAP creator, its interface/options, the pac creator, the H0 creation-rate probe and PRQ-C-04, `dataverseDisplayName`, H5's region/tier inputs) unless something else reads it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">Real HTTP against hand-written handlers; never Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Intake: `subscriptionId` required for every model; new `dataverseEnvUrl` (https, `*.dynamics.com` origin, host label per the naming rule); `containerTypeId` required GUID (G19); schema + catalog + endpoint parity; tests.</step>
    <step order="2">H1: subscription tenant matches the run's tenant; no other customer's `rg-spaarke-*`; tests.</step>
    <step order="3">H5 → adopt: read `dataverseEnvUrl`, enforce the host rule, prove reachability as the Worker identity (WhoAmI; 401/403 → Resumable naming the prerequisite), write `DataverseEnvUrl`; delete the creation code; DAG: H10 ← H3, H5; H6 ← H5, H3, H10; H8 ← H3, H5, H10; H11 ← H10, H7; tests (incl. DAG parity / run-context contract).</step>
    <step order="4">ArmDeploymentRunner Model 1 → `customer`; controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep → Owner at the customer subscription; platform-controlplane.bicep stops deploying it; recompile JSON where tracked.</step>
    <step order="5">prereqs.yaml (subscription exists + dedicated; PRQ-S-04 Owner via the module; operator creates the environment + adds the L2 Worker identity as System Administrator application user; PRQ-C-04 retired), skill (Step 1 prompts subscriptionId + dataverseEnvUrl; remove Step 1e and the az-account default; registry row gets the real URL), guide/inventory/constraints.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify (ControlPlane tests, ArchTests, Worker + Api builds, bicep build); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">CreateRun returns 400 for a Model 1 or Model 2 request without `subscriptionId`, without/with a malformed `dataverseEnvUrl`, or without/with a non-GUID `containerTypeId`; schema and endpoint agree (parity tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H1: another tenant's subscription → Resumable refusal; a subscription with `rg-spaarke-{otherCustomer}-{env}` → Resumable refusal naming it; this customer's own RG is accepted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H5 never calls a creation API (the code is gone); host rule violation → Resumable; WhoAmI 401/403 → Resumable naming the Worker-app-user prerequisite; reachable → DataverseEnvUrl written and completed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DAG: H10 precedes H6 and H8; no cycle; run-context contract green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Model 1 resolves the `customer` template; no "Model 1 not deployable" path remains.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git grep` finds no shared/default subscription for Model 1 in src, scripts, the skill or the schema; Step 1e is gone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane.Tests, ArchTests pass; Worker/Api build with 0 warnings; bicep builds.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Something other than H5 turns out to need Dataverse environment creation (a reader of the creator or rate probe).</trigger>
    <trigger>A live action would be required to verify (role assignment, environment creation) — ask the owner first.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes/>
</task>
